.TH STATUS-MU2EDAQ-NOTIFY-PROXY.SH 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-phone-notification-system 0.1.0" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
status-mu2edaq-notify-proxy.sh \- report the state of every link in the public notification chain
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B scripts/status\-mu2edaq\-notify\-proxy.sh
.SH DESCRIPTION
Read\-only. Prints one line each for: the local server and tunnel pid files;
the instance's public IPv4 from the EC2 API; the public name's DNS answer and
whether it matches
.RB ( STALE
when it does not); the CAA record's pinned ACME account; remote
.B caddy
and
.B mu2edaq\-notify\-dns.timer
state over SSH; and the HTTP status of the public
.B /api/health
(8 s timeout).
.PP
The pid\-file lines only see processes started by the start scripts; a server
or tunnel run by its launchd agent shows as
.BR "no pid file" .
.SH OPTIONS
None.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.BR MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_SERVER_PIDFILE ,
.BR MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_PROXY_PIDFILE ,
.BR MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_PUBLIC_URL ,
.BR MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_PROXY_USER ,
.BR MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_PROXY_KEY ,
.BR MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_PROXY_DNS_NAME ,
.BR MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_ROUTE53_ZONE_ID ,
and the shared defaults in
.IR scripts/notify-proxy-common.sh .
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
Always 0; read the output. It is not a monitoring probe \(em use
.B update\-notify\-dns.sh \-\-check
or
.B restore\-mu2edaq\-notify\-tunnel.sh \-\-check
for that.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
scripts/status\-mu2edaq\-notify\-proxy.sh
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR start-mu2edaq-notify-chain.sh (1),
.BR update-notify-dns.sh (1),
.BR update-notify-caa.sh (1),
.BR restore-mu2edaq-notify-tunnel.sh (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Mu2e DAQ Group. Part of
.BR mu2edaq-phone-notification-system .
